<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harald Hardrada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1015–1066</span> · Also known as Harald III of Norway, Harald Sigurdsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harald Hardrada (Harald Sigurdsson) was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1046 to 1066. A half-brother of Olaf II, he served for years in the Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varangian-guard">Varangian Guard</a> before returning to share and then hold the Norwegian throne. He fought a long war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and was killed invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-stamford-bridge">Battle of Stamford Bridge</a> in 1066.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada.jpg" alt="Harald Hardrada" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zeichner: C. I. Schive, Lithograf Bucher in Bergen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harold-III-Coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
